    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0206" n="158" xml:id="pg158"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2139.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-03-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 6, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch of the 5th of February, No. 1531, which relates to the case of Michael
                    McKeen, arrested at Queenstown on suspicion, and subsequently released. Your
                    suggestions concerning the importance of United States citizens who may visit
                    Great Britain being provided with evidences of citizenship, are approved. In
                    this connection, I inclose a copy of an executive order of the 18th ultimo on
                    that subject.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d42-a1.xml" xpointer="d42-a1"/>
            </div>
